# Rapid Reload, WITHOUT the feat. inc-l59x.
#
# Load the frozen Warrior who has NO FT_RAPID_RELOAD and equip him with an
# arbalest, then crank it once. Paired with tools/keys/rapid-reload-feat.keys;
# tools/check_rapid_reload.sh compares the two crank costs.
#
# This character's arbalest is buried in his backpack, so he is put into
# wizard mode and a fresh arbalest is drawn from Item Acquisition straight
# into the Weapon Hand, the way tools/keys/prestige-masterarcher.keys does.
# The `@until "]: Missile Weapons"` walks the acquisition tabs to Missile
# Weapons and `DOWN*2` reaches the arbalest row.
#
# `w y` enters wizard mode; the game then asks its own "Enter wizard mode?"
# prompt, answered `y`. The `s` buys the real turn a loaded session needs.

@dump:arrival
s
@dump:searched

w
y
@choose "Item Acquisition"
@until "]: Missile Weapons" RIGHT
DOWN*2
ENTER
b SPACE                 # the arbalest into the Weapon Hand
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
@dump:wielded

f                       # fire: the uncocked crossbow is cranked instead
@dump:reloaded

@quit
